WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.450
I would love to tell a Norm story since-

00:00:01.450 --> 00:00:02.283
Yeah, yeah.

00:00:02.283 --> 00:00:06.390
You really moved me at the
memorial and I love Norm.

00:00:06.390 --> 00:00:11.390
He was my, when I was a very,
very beginning comedian,

00:00:12.180 --> 00:00:16.408
my first real legit road gig was MCing,

00:00:16.408 --> 00:00:20.010
his seven or eight shows

00:00:20.010 --> 00:00:21.690
of Catch a Rising Star in Princeton.

00:00:21.690 --> 00:00:23.790
This would've been about like '90-91.

00:00:23.790 --> 00:00:25.080
Norm was not famous.

00:00:25.080 --> 00:00:29.160
He was this sort of like hot-young comic

00:00:29.160 --> 00:00:31.590
coming out of Canada.

00:00:31.590 --> 00:00:32.760
And he wasn't famous here.

00:00:32.760 --> 00:00:33.660
He hadn't done Letterman.

00:00:33.660 --> 00:00:35.283
He hadn't done really much here.

00:00:35.283 --> 00:00:37.533
And it was a big gig for me.

00:00:38.460 --> 00:00:41.880
And I'm hosting Norm shows.

00:00:41.880 --> 00:00:44.910
And this is when Andrew Dice-Clay
was the number one comic

00:00:44.910 --> 00:00:46.050
in the world.

00:00:46.050 --> 00:00:48.720
And Norm was so different than that.

00:00:48.720 --> 00:00:49.740
Yes, yeah.

00:00:49.740 --> 00:00:51.360
But comedy was hot.

00:00:51.360 --> 00:00:54.210
So the club was packed every night

00:00:54.210 --> 00:00:55.890
and Norm had this weird accent

00:00:55.890 --> 00:01:00.150
and his jokes were long
and they were often absurd.

00:01:00.150 --> 00:01:05.150
And you know, the crowd was seven shows.

00:01:05.460 --> 00:01:07.890
He probably bombed three of them.

00:01:07.890 --> 00:01:09.030
And he killed the other four.

00:01:09.030 --> 00:01:10.560
They either got him, they either loved him

00:01:10.560 --> 00:01:11.610
or they hated him.

00:01:11.610 --> 00:01:15.240
And when he killed, we'd go backstage

00:01:15.240 --> 00:01:17.730
and we would play poker
until the next show.

00:01:17.730 --> 00:01:21.930
When he bombed inexplicably,
he would go to the exit

00:01:21.930 --> 00:01:24.541
and say goodbye to every single person.

00:01:24.541 --> 00:01:27.124
(group laughs)

00:01:30.174 --> 00:01:31.380
I think to entertain me,

00:01:31.380 --> 00:01:34.350
I don't know if he just
loved the awkwardness

00:01:34.350 --> 00:01:37.860
of it or he was always
one step ahead of me.

00:01:37.860 --> 00:01:40.800
One step ahead of his vans, the industry,

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:45.800
I wish he had been been, he
wanted to tell the most honest,

00:01:45.900 --> 00:01:47.520
the most brutally funny joke

00:01:47.520 --> 00:01:49.500
no matter what the consequences,

00:01:49.500 --> 00:01:53.032
I would play poker with him
later on when he was at SNL,

00:01:53.032 --> 00:01:55.920
he would have the guys over on Mondays

00:01:55.920 --> 00:01:57.450
when whatever it was Sundays,

00:01:57.450 --> 00:01:59.280
whenever there was no one up there

00:01:59.280 --> 00:02:01.590
and we'd play poker and he
liked to play poker there

00:02:01.590 --> 00:02:04.560
'cause he had the long table
and he could watch five TVs,

00:02:04.560 --> 00:02:05.912
so he could gamble on football.

00:02:05.912 --> 00:02:06.745
Yep.

00:02:06.745 --> 00:02:10.320
While playing poker and
while holding court.

00:02:10.320 --> 00:02:12.600
And it was so much fun for me.

00:02:12.600 --> 00:02:14.010
And then he said, come back Saturday,

00:02:14.010 --> 00:02:15.120
come hang out at the show.

00:02:15.120 --> 00:02:18.000
So this is an example of Norm

00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:20.760
just not giving a flying
fuck about anybody.

00:02:20.760 --> 00:02:23.040
Like he just wanted to
make people laugh no matter

00:02:23.040 --> 00:02:27.690
what the consequences and
Rosie O'Donnell was the host

00:02:27.690 --> 00:02:30.420
of the show that week, a guest guest host

00:02:30.420 --> 00:02:33.900
and height of her fame
with Penny Marshall.

00:02:33.900 --> 00:02:36.870
They were this famous team

00:02:36.870 --> 00:02:38.429
and they'd done a big movie together.

00:02:38.429 --> 00:02:43.429
And penny by now is a big movie director.

00:02:45.030 --> 00:02:47.640
And I'm in that hallway,
where the pages are,

00:02:47.640 --> 00:02:51.600
where the desk is, and
everybody kind of congregates

00:02:51.600 --> 00:02:52.433
in that area.

00:02:52.433 --> 00:02:53.266
It's crowded.

00:02:53.266 --> 00:02:56.760
It's 10 minutes to show
time and I'm standing there

00:02:56.760 --> 00:02:59.490
with Norm and a bunch of writers
and pages and whoever else

00:02:59.490 --> 00:03:02.310
and our guests and Penny
comes in with a baseball hat

00:03:02.310 --> 00:03:06.030
and sunglasses head down just
kind of big timing everybody,

00:03:06.030 --> 00:03:08.970
just cutting through the
crowd, celebrity style

00:03:08.970 --> 00:03:12.150
and Norm starts going,

00:03:12.150 --> 00:03:14.850
starts pointing at her and
screaming Laverne, Laverne.

00:03:16.599 --> 00:03:19.182
(group laughs)

00:03:23.735 --> 00:03:28.735
A month later, I think he was
fired for telling OJ jokes

00:03:29.070 --> 00:03:30.480
but it really shows

00:03:30.480 --> 00:03:33.300
that he just wanted to
tell the best jokes.

00:03:33.300 --> 00:03:35.670
I wish he was so brutally
honest about his health.

00:03:35.670 --> 00:03:37.500
We would've gotten to say goodbye to him.

00:03:37.500 --> 00:03:38.333
I know.

00:03:38.333 --> 00:03:39.592
A proper send off.

00:03:39.592 --> 00:03:40.425
I think that bothered a lot of us.

00:03:40.425 --> 00:03:41.310
And I think a lot of us assumed

00:03:41.310 --> 00:03:43.440
everyone knew when it happened.

00:03:43.440 --> 00:03:45.496
I thought, oh Jesus, he didn't tell me

00:03:45.496 --> 00:03:48.420
but I guess I would assume you would know.

00:03:48.420 --> 00:03:50.130
We all assumed everyone else knew.

00:03:50.130 --> 00:03:52.200
And then it turned out that nobody knew,

00:03:52.200 --> 00:03:55.890
his family knew and Lori
Joe knew, but that was,

00:03:55.890 --> 00:03:57.540
he didn't want people to know.

00:03:57.540 --> 00:03:59.692
That's what he wanted,
so I guess you have to-

00:03:59.692 --> 00:04:00.525
I get it.

00:04:00.525 --> 00:04:02.790
I had fricking a skin condition,

00:04:02.790 --> 00:04:04.590
I didn't want anyone to know.

00:04:04.590 --> 00:04:08.010
Anything that makes you think
the audience might feel sorry

00:04:08.010 --> 00:04:11.850
or sympathy or not
think you're just funny.

00:04:11.850 --> 00:04:13.980
Anything that undercuts the comedy

00:04:13.980 --> 00:04:15.420
you don't want the audience to know.

00:04:15.420 --> 00:04:16.323
So I get it.

